Post-Installation Setup for Metasploit Framework
================================================

Metasploit uses a PostgreSQL database to store workspaces, hosts, services
and vulnerabilities. This package does NOT create or start any database
automatically; you set it up yourself as a regular user (NOT root):

    $ msfdb init

By default msfdb creates a private PostgreSQL cluster in ~/.msf4/db, owned
by your user, so the system-wide postgresql runit service is NOT required.
The database client and server tools (psql, createdb, initdb, pg_ctl) are
pulled in by the 'postgresql' and 'postgresql-client' dependencies.

Useful commands:

    $ msfdb status      # show database state
    $ msfdb start       # start your private database
    $ msfdb stop        # stop it

To verify the connection:

    $ msfconsole
    msf6 > db_status

Using the system-wide PostgreSQL service instead (optional, advanced):
enable it with 'ln -s /etc/sv/postgresql /var/service/', initialise the
cluster yourself, and pass --connection-string to msfdb. Note that the
default 'initdb' settings allow passwordless local connections, so review
pg_hba.conf before using it on a multi-user machine.

For more information, see:
https://docs.metasploit.com/docs/using-metasploit/getting-started/setting-up-a-metasploit-database.html
